WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.490 --> 00:00:01.345
Name a pattern.

2
00:00:01.365 --> 00:00:02.805
Now defend it.

3
00:00:02.825 --> 00:00:05.905
A staff answer knows the problem each pattern solves.

4
00:00:05.925 --> 00:00:07.490
And what it costs.

5
00:00:07.510 --> 00:00:10.190
Four patterns come up most: Lambda and Kappa,

6
00:00:10.210 --> 00:00:13.890
medallion layers, the outbox, and data mesh.

7
00:00:13.910 --> 00:00:16.150
First: batch, stream, or both?

8
00:00:16.170 --> 00:00:17.812
Lambda runs two paths.

9
00:00:17.832 --> 00:00:21.360
A fast stream for now, and a batch for the correct result.

10
00:00:21.380 --> 00:00:25.520
The cost: you write the same logic twice, and keep both in step.

11
00:00:25.540 --> 00:00:27.295
Kappa keeps only the stream.

12
00:00:27.315 --> 00:00:30.320
To fix history, you replay the log.

13
00:00:30.340 --> 00:00:32.780
Second: bronze, silver, gold.

14
00:00:32.800 --> 00:00:35.105
Bronze is the raw data, as it arrived.

15
00:00:35.125 --> 00:00:36.492
Silver is clean.

16
00:00:36.512 --> 00:00:38.715
Gold is ready for the business.

17
00:00:38.735 --> 00:00:40.365
Keep bronze unchanged.

18
00:00:40.385 --> 00:00:43.915
Then you can rebuild silver and gold at any time.

19
00:00:43.935 --> 00:00:47.275
Third: save to the database, and publish an event.

20
00:00:47.295 --> 00:00:49.800
If you do the two steps apart, one can fail.

21
00:00:49.820 --> 00:00:51.885
Then the systems disagree.

22
00:00:51.905 --> 00:00:55.745
So write the event to an outbox table, in the same transaction.

23
00:00:55.765 --> 00:00:58.770
A separate process reads the outbox and publishes.

24
00:00:58.790 --> 00:01:00.970
Nothing is lost.

25
00:01:00.990 --> 00:01:03.080
Last: who owns the data?

26
00:01:03.100 --> 00:01:07.290
In a data mesh, each domain team owns its data as a product.

27
00:01:07.310 --> 00:01:08.715
It fits a large company.

28
00:01:08.735 --> 00:01:10.965
For a small team, it is too much overhead.

29
00:01:10.985 --> 00:01:12.715
Say no.

30
00:01:12.735 --> 00:01:14.800
Quick recap of the patterns.

31
00:01:14.820 --> 00:01:16.712
Lambda costs two code paths.

32
00:01:16.732 --> 00:01:17.825
Keep bronze raw.

33
00:01:17.845 --> 00:01:20.185
And use an outbox for two writes.

34
00:01:20.205 --> 00:01:23.305
Now start the first lesson below.
